  "question": {
    "text": "Let the points $\\left(\\frac{11}{2}, \\alpha\\right)$ lie on or inside the triangle with sides $x+y=11, x+2 y=16$ and $2 x+3 y=29$. Then the product of the smallest and the largest values of $\\alpha$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EZyjh",
      "text": "44",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Y6FXj",
      "text": "22",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Bx2kp",
      "text": "33",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HH9tT",
      "text": "55",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/iM9WDDi4qmrkBX2YtLLqEuIW0CodQiJCCWa5vnlX8Mk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nClearly, $x=\\frac{11}{2}$ intersect $x+y-11=0$ at $\\left(\\frac{11}{2}, \\frac{11}{2}\\right)$ and $2 x+3 y-29=0$ at $\\left(\\frac{11}{2}, 6\\right) \\Rightarrow \\alpha=\\left[\\frac{11}{2}, 6\\right]$\n$\\alpha_{\\min } \\cdot \\alpha_{\\max }=\\frac{11}{2} \\cdot 6=33$",
    "image": null
  },
